# Wrangler / Cloudflare
.wrangler/
.dev.vars

# Secrets. `.env` is NOT tracked: a real key committed here is world-readable
# forever, even after a later commit blanks it out. That is exactly how the
# previous Giphy key ended up banned. Keep the template in `.env.example`
# (values blank) and set real secrets in the hosting environment instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

